## 2. Protocol items (as the documents give them)
### Film (I3 §1.1 table; CFG films.yaml)
- Caminandes 3, 2016, animation, CC BY 3.0, Blender, split dev, 2.5 min, 37 shots, 0 dialogue lines (I3 §1.1). CFG: id `caminandes3`, page `https://archive.org/details/CaminandesLlamigos`, `master_sha256: 028d7629782251a212986662b50445daa2ee278aff279a4af8bd02dde28f8d7f` (CFG `films.yaml`; the backup `/crewcut/masters/caminandes3.ogv` hashes to the same value). I3 §1.6: pinned file is an Internet Archive auto-transcoded small `.ogv`, not the largest file.
- Admission needs all of (I3 §1.2): licence CC0/CC BY/CC BY-SA or US public domain; no NC/ND; no third-party-held content (music, songs, source works) — manual judgment; PD basis explicit; a fixed master file with checksum. Trailers/extras are never candidates.
- I3 §1.6 probe on this film: 36 cut points all agree with published; dialogue and hierarchy identical; 90 task IDs identical.
### Annotations (I3 §1.3)
shots (frame no. and time of each cut, automatic), dialogue (start/end/text, ASR), shot description (1–3 sentences "[景别] 的 [主体] [动作]，[运镜]", characters as C1, C2…, no colour/lens/style; VLM-drafted), hierarchy L0–L4 (derived), provenance fingerprints (frame + audio, from master). Speaker/character/description corrections: out of scope.
### Hierarchy (I3 §1.4; CFG benchmark.yaml same values)
- L0 shot. L1 beat: 2–8 consecutive shots in one scene, ≤40 s; a shot >40 s or a lone shot is its own beat (CFG: min_shots 2, max_shots 8, max_seconds 40).
- L2 scene: boundary where each of the 3 shots before and after are mutually dissimilar by shot-appearance similarity; scenes <12 s merge into previous (CFG: link_window_shots 3, kappa 1.0, min_seconds 12 — kappa is only in CFG).
- L3: 2–6 scenes, ≤10 min; over-long single scene alone (CFG max_scenes 6, max_seconds 600). L4 whole film, only ≤15 min (CFG max_seconds 900).
- Sampling: L0 30 shots, L1 15 beats, duration-stratified, seed determined by the film; fewer → all (CFG sample_per_film L0 30, L1 15).
- Tasks: every L2/L3/L4 segment; sampled L0/L1; two tracks per segment: Reference (`ref`) and Screenplay (`scr`). Dev totals (all films): L0 155/310, L1 69/138, L2 56/112, L3 14/28, L4 5/10; 299 segments/598 tasks. (Caminandes 3: 90 task IDs, I3 §1.6.)
- Task contents: instructions, delivery spec, tool list of the tier, budget per minute of segment: model $20, tools $5, 1 h wall clock, at least 15 min (CFG wall_clock_floor_minutes 15); input (Screenplay: script of dialogue+times and shot table of times+descriptions); the segment's answer (cuts, shots+descriptions, dialogue, scenes) used only for scoring and never visible to the system.
### Run rules (I3 §2.1–2.3)
- `fixed`: no agent, no feedback loop; one still frame + slow push per shot, one synthetic voice per speaker, one background music, cut at the cut points; leaderboard floor.
- Isolation; no answer visible; all model calls metered; all generator calls through one tool server charging fixed prices and refusing inputs from the original film; uniform event log.
- Tiers: T0 image generate/edit, speech, music, sfx, video edit; T1 = T0 + Wan 2.2 video; T2 own generators. CFG tools.yaml defines profile `smoke` (all generators replaced by placeholder, runs marked unofficial) — see gaps G1.
- Delivery: MP4 H.264 1280×720 24 fps; AAC stereo 48 kHz; English WebVTT; manifest of used assets; duration within ±5% of the segment (CFG: yuv420p, tolerance 0.05).
- Runs per task: 3 (L4: 2) (I3 §2.4; CFG runs). For this round only one run is asked? — gaps G4.
### Scoring (I3 §2.4)
R = (Q, Q·c, Q·S, $). Q (pass/fail): decodes fully with picture and sound; format per spec; duration within ±5%; subtitles cover every dialogue line; log shows no generator read original input; provenance check finds no original frame/audio. Q fail ⇒ c and S zero.
c: cut F1 at tolerance 0.5 s and 1.0 s; shot correspondence (judge sees only the original shot description and 1 frame/s of the remake's same period, 2–8 frames; match or not; duration-weighted); dialogue WER and onset-time error; speaker/character consistency (cluster purity); scene order. Judge must be a different vendor from the system's base model.
S (screening) — out of scope this round. $: total cost etc.; budget stats are in I3, reported as run data.
CFG continuity: cut_tolerance_s [0.5, 1.0]; frames/second 1, min 2, max 8. CFG provenance: frame_sample_fps 2, phash_max_hamming 10, dino_min_cosine 0.92, audio_min_match 0.35, max_false_flag_rate 0.01 (I3 §2.5 says thresholds are set on the stress test; values in CFG only).
### Release / evidence (I3 §1.5)
Master verified by checksum; annotations, descriptions with model recorded, fingerprints, task packages; evidence of agreement with `d509bed` (cuts, dialogue, hierarchy, task list), every difference listed and explained; README states verified status.

